WEBVTT

00:00.350 --> 00:06.308
Pharmaceutical quality teams work through controlled procedures, work
instructions, validation summaries and change records.

00:06.308 --> 00:15.246
Before a quality decision is approved, the reviewer needs the current source,
the applicable wording and a defensible record of what

00:15.246 --> 00:16.097
was checked.

00:16.097 --> 00:21.630
When that trail is fragmented, experienced people spend valuable time
reconstructing documentary context.

00:22.630 --> 00:29.302
A single quality process can depend on a standard operating procedure, linked
work instructions, validation material, approved change

00:29.302 --> 00:30.785
controls and historic revisions.

00:30.785 --> 00:32.267
A clause can move.

00:32.267 --> 00:34.121
A reference can be replaced.

00:34.121 --> 00:38.198
An effective date can change what applied at a particular time.

00:38.198 --> 00:41.534
The review problem is not simply finding a phrase.

00:41.534 --> 00:44.870
It is establishing the controlled relationship between the sources.

00:45.870 --> 00:50.030
Choose one non-production quality workflow and agree the authoritative corpus.

00:50.030 --> 00:55.438
Define the users, access boundary, test questions and evidence standard before
evaluation begins.

00:55.438 --> 01:00.846
Include difficult documents, superseded wording, absent references and
questions the system should refuse.

01:00.846 --> 01:08.750
Compare the same tasks against the current review process, rather than
treating a polished demonstration as proof of fitness.

01:09.750 --> 01:15.311
Cortessa is intended to run on a dedicated sovereign workstation inside an
agreed boundary.

01:15.311 --> 01:20.873
The approved corpus, local index, on-device model and source viewer remain
within that environment.

01:20.873 --> 01:24.845
Runtime operation does not depend on a public cloud service.

01:24.845 --> 01:29.215
The organisation defines permitted documents, users, identity controls and
security posture.

01:29.215 --> 01:32.790
Cortessa does not become the quality system of record.

01:33.790 --> 01:36.924
Audit is the centre of the Cortessa workflow.

01:36.924 --> 01:43.583
It works across the bounded quality corpus to surface a missing reference,
inconsistent terminology, uncertain effectivity, unexplained

01:43.583 --> 01:48.676
revision differences or a procedure that appears to rely on a superseded
source.

01:48.676 --> 01:51.418
Each candidate enters a controlled review queue.

01:51.418 --> 01:56.510
It is not automatically treated as a deviation or a finding of non-compliance.

01:57.510 --> 02:01.974
Each audit result leads back to the passage that created it.

02:01.974 --> 02:08.061
Quality specialists can open the source, inspect surrounding wording and
confirm revision and document state.

02:08.061 --> 02:13.336
If the evidence is absent, Cortessa can refuse rather than fill the gap.

02:13.336 --> 02:20.640
Authorised quality personnel determine relevance, accept or reject the
candidate, and record the outcome through the existing process.

02:20.640 --> 02:25.510
Verified shows provenance; it does not establish GMP compliance or validation
status.

02:26.510 --> 02:34.242
Process context, product impact and the organisation's quality framework
cannot be delegated to a language model.

02:34.242 --> 02:38.108
Cortessa can expose the evidence route and uncertainty.

02:38.108 --> 02:42.941
Authorised quality personnel determine applicability, significance and the
required action.

02:42.941 --> 02:50.190
Cortessa does not release batches, replace the qualified person, validate
itself or provide MHRA approval.

02:51.190 --> 02:56.969
Reviewers need the source route, document state and the policy governing what
the system may present.

02:56.969 --> 03:01.304
Identity, document currency, assertion policy and egress posture remain
visible governance concerns.

03:01.304 --> 03:08.167
Local activity can be recorded in a ledger so the organisation can inspect
what the system did and when.

03:08.167 --> 03:15.030
The record can support an evidence package, but it does not replace approved
quality records or establish data-integrity compliance.

03:16.030 --> 03:22.452
Measure time to the current approved source, citation completeness,
supersession visibility, accepted and rejected findings, correct

03:22.452 --> 03:24.058
refusals and reviewer effort.

03:24.058 --> 03:26.466
Record corpus preparation and setup burden.

03:26.466 --> 03:34.092
The result should show where Cortessa helps, where it fails and what must be
remediated before any next stage.

03:34.092 --> 03:39.310
Evidence from the customer's own workflow is more valuable than a generic
claim.

03:40.310 --> 03:46.030
Bring one bounded, non-production quality workflow and the people authorised
to judge it.

03:46.030 --> 03:51.310
Evaluate the evidence route, remediate observed gaps and retest before
considering expansion.

03:51.310 --> 03:53.510
Start a conversation with Cortessa.
